<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bheemunipatnam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bimlipatnam</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bheemunipatnam, also known as Bimlipatnam, is a coastal town north of Visakhapatnam in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In the 17th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> established a trading post there, part of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coromandel-coast">Coromandel</a> governorate, dealing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> cloth and other goods. The ruins of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fort and its cemetery survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bheemunipatnam.jpg" alt="Bheemunipatnam" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adityamadhav83 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_View_of_Bheemunipatnam_Hilltop_Visakhapatnam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
